      "rules": [
        {
          "group_id_src": "V-204636",
          "group_tree": [
            {
              "id": "V-204636",
              "title": "SRG-APP-000023",
              "description": "<GroupDescription></GroupDescription>"
            }
          ],
          "group_id": "V-204636",
          "severity": "medium",
          "group_title": "SRG-APP-000023",
          "rule_id_src": "SV-204636r1043176_rule",
          "rule_id": "SV-204636r1043176",
          "rule_version": "SRG-APP-000023-AAA-000030",
          "rule_title": "AAA Services must be configured to provide automated account management functions.",
          "fix_text": "Configure AAA Services to provide automated account management functions. Automated functions include disabling accounts after specified periods of inactivity, locking accounts after a specified number of incorrect logon attempts, etc. Where possible, automated functions must be performed on users and devices globally rather than by each individual account.",
          "weight": "10.0",
          "check_content": "If AAA Services rely on directory services for user account management, this is not applicable and the connected directory services must perform this function.\n\nVerify AAA Services are configured to provide automated account management functions. Automated functions include disabling accounts after specified periods of inactivity, locking accounts after a specified number of incorrect logon attempts, etc. Where possible, automated functions must be performed on users and devices globally rather than by each individual account.\n\nIf AAA Services do not provide automated account management functions, this is a finding.",
          "check_content_ref": {
            "href": "AAA_Services_SRG.xml",
            "name": "M"
          },
          "classification": "Unclassified",
          "discussion": "Enterprise environments make account management challenging and complex. A manual process for account management functions adds the risk of a potential oversight or other error. A comprehensive account management process that includes automation helps to ensure accounts designated as requiring attention are consistently and promptly addressed. Examples include, but are not limited to, using automation to disable inactive accounts after a specified time period, or to lock accounts after a specified number of unsuccessful attempts at logon.\n\nAAA Services must be configured to automatically provide account management functions, and these functions must immediately enforce the organization's current account policy. The automated mechanisms may reside within AAA Services or may be directory services providing automated account management externally. Automated mechanisms may be composed of differing technologies that when placed together contain an overall automated mechanism supporting an organization's automated account management requirements. \n\nAccount management functions include assignment of role membership; identifying account type; specifying user access authorizations (i.e., privileges); account removal, update, or termination; and administrative alerts. The use of automated mechanisms can include, for example, using email or text messaging to automatically notifying account managers when users are terminated or transferred; using the information system to monitor account usage; and using automated telephonic notification to report atypical system account usage.",
          "false_positives": "",
          "false_negatives": "",
          "documentable": "false",
          "security_override_guidance": "",
          "potential_impacts": "",
          "third_party_tools": "",
          "ia_controls": "",
          "responsibility": "",
          "mitigations": "",
          "mitigation_control": "",
          "legacy_ids": [
            "SV-95529",
            "V-80819"
          ],
          "ccis": [
            "CCI-000015"
          ],
          "reference_identifier": "2896",
          "uuid": "b900c4f6-fa35-5861-88e5-68530e9323ef",
          "stig_uuid": "48d52574-4cd5-5714-881e-63304d1f3ea9",
          "status": "not_reviewed",
          "overrides": {},
          "comments": "Assessment recommendation: Likely covered\nEvidence state: source-inferred\nAssessed release: 2026.45.4-uds.1\nHorizon commit: b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c\n\nJustification: Actual delivered identity profile delegates account management to shared UDS. Its configured three-failure permanent lockout is an automatic global account-management function, satisfying the broad capability requirement. Exact inactivity and temporary-account requirements are assessed separately; an API implementation duplicating the IdP is not needed.\n\nComponents: UDS Core 1.14 shared Keycloak realm and Horizon OIDC clients; no bundled application Keycloak\n\nOwner: Gallatin SRE (self-managed UDS Core on MPN)\n\nNext action: Maintain the cited source/configuration mapping for the selected release and reassess any Gallatin deployment overrides that change this control.\n\nEvidence:\n[re-aaa-release] re-aaa-release\nSuccessful UDS publication artifact horizon-release-2026.45.4-uds.1 platform-contract.json selects identity.mode=uds, issuer https://sso.uds.dev/realms/uds, Core1.14.0; build-info.json enumerates12 deliveredimages and no bundled Keycloak.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon-uds-bundle/actions/runs/42114745685\n\n[re-aaa-realm] re-aaa-realm\nRealm has failureFactor3, permanentLockout true, maxTemporaryLockouts0; password length15,upper/lower/digit,special2,history5 and expiry60days; jsonlog listener emits user/admin events. Browser has password and X509 alternative authentication; X509MFA defaultdisabled. Account-inactivity workflow optionaldisabled; no minimum-age/difference/blacklist policy selected. Recovery flow requires reset-password.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-identity-config/blob/74480722e1cc8405b5e9b65ac7d7086ab7f4056d/src/realm.json5\n\n[re-aaa-values] re-aaa-values\nCore uses identity-config0.32, X509/OTP enabled, username/password enabled; X509_MFA false, inactivity flag unset, detailed-observability alertingdisabled. Insecure admin password generation disabled. Truststore includes UDS bundle and serviceaccount CA separately from configimage truststore.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/keycloak/chart/values.yaml\n\n[mpn-identity-values] mpn-identity-values\nCore1.14 chart default fields: realmInitEnv.SSO_SESSION_MAX_PER_USER=\"0\"; ACCOUNT_INACTIVITY_DAYS unset; terms enabled unset; detailedObservability.alerts.enabled=false; realmAuthFlows username/password/X509/OTPtrue, X509MFAfalse. Gallatin owns these settings on MPN, independent of DU managedIL5/IL6 clusters.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/keycloak/chart/values.yaml\n\n[mpn-identity-override] mpn-identity-override\nCore value sourcePath .keycloak.keycloak maps to chart root; bundle override path is packages[core].overrides.keycloak.keycloak.values[].path (e.g.realmInitEnv), not Horizonpackageapplication values.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/keycloak/common/zarf.yaml",
          "finding_details": "Recommendation: Likely covered. Actual delivered identity profile delegates account management to shared UDS. Its configured three-failure permanent lockout is an automatic global account-management function, satisfying the broad capability requirement. Exact inactivity and temporary-account requirements are assessed separately; an API implementation duplicating the IdP is not needed.\n\nNext action: Maintain the cited source/configuration mapping for the selected release and reassess any Gallatin deployment overrides that change this control."
        },
        {
          "group_id_src": "V-204637",
          "group_tree": [
            {
              "id": "V-204637",
              "title": "SRG-APP-000024",
              "description": "<GroupDescription></GroupDescription>"
            }
          ],
          "group_id": "V-204637",
          "severity": "medium",
          "group_title": "SRG-APP-000024",
          "rule_id_src": "SV-204637r960771_rule",
          "rule_id": "SV-204637r960771",
          "rule_version": "SRG-APP-000024-AAA-000040",
          "rule_title": "AAA Services must be configured to automatically remove temporary user accounts after 72 hours.",
          "fix_text": "Configure AAA Services to automatically remove temporary user accounts after 72 hours.",
          "weight": "10.0",
          "check_content": "If AAA Services rely on directory services for user account management, this is not applicable and the connected directory services must perform this function. \n\nVerify AAA Services are configured to automatically remove temporary user accounts after 72 hours.\n\nIf the AAA Services configuration does not automatically remove temporary user accounts after 72 hours, this is a finding.",
          "check_content_ref": {
            "href": "AAA_Services_SRG.xml",
            "name": "M"
          },
          "classification": "Unclassified",
          "discussion": "When temporary user accounts remain active after no longer needed or for an excessive period, these accounts may be used to gain unauthorized access. To mitigate this risk, automated termination of all temporary user accounts must be set upon account creation. Disabling a temporary account provides a higher risk alternative; disabling allows an insider adversary to enable the privileged account and make it permanent.\n\nTemporary accounts, when used, mandate that AAA Services must be configured to automatically terminate these types of accounts after 72 hours. When AAA Services do not perform account management, the connected Active Directory must provide this setting.",
          "false_positives": "",
          "false_negatives": "",
          "documentable": "false",
          "security_override_guidance": "",
          "potential_impacts": "",
          "third_party_tools": "",
          "ia_controls": "",
          "responsibility": "",
          "mitigations": "",
          "mitigation_control": "",
          "legacy_ids": [
            "SV-95661",
            "V-80951"
          ],
          "ccis": [
            "CCI-000016"
          ],
          "reference_identifier": "2896",
          "uuid": "dc136b87-c1b6-5088-a615-2672ca30addc",
          "stig_uuid": "48d52574-4cd5-5714-881e-63304d1f3ea9",
          "status": "not_reviewed",
          "overrides": {},
          "comments": "Assessment recommendation: Needs N/A justification\nEvidence state: source-inferred\nAssessed release: 2026.45.4-uds.1\nHorizon commit: b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c\n\nJustification: Delivered Horizon delegates all human identities to shared UDS and defines no temporary-user creation/type or72-hour temporary-account lifecycle. Configure expiry at the shared identity provider where applicable. Record that temporary accounts are prohibited/unused in the assessed realm; if they are permitted, the UDS operator must configure their expiration/removal.\n\nComponents: UDS Core 1.14 shared Keycloak realm and Horizon OIDC clients; no bundled application Keycloak\n\nOwner: Gallatin SRE (self-managed UDS Core on MPN)\n\nNext action: Record the temporary-account applicability policy; configure72-hour removal only if those accounts are allowed.\n\nEvidence:\n[re-aaa-release] re-aaa-release\nSuccessful UDS publication artifact horizon-release-2026.45.4-uds.1 platform-contract.json selects identity.mode=uds, issuer https://sso.uds.dev/realms/uds, Core1.14.0; build-info.json enumerates12 deliveredimages and no bundled Keycloak.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon-uds-bundle/actions/runs/42114745685\n\n[re-aaa-realm] re-aaa-realm\nRealm has failureFactor3, permanentLockout true, maxTemporaryLockouts0; password length15,upper/lower/digit,special2,history5 and expiry60days; jsonlog listener emits user/admin events. Browser has password and X509 alternative authentication; X509MFA defaultdisabled. Account-inactivity workflow optionaldisabled; no minimum-age/difference/blacklist policy selected. Recovery flow requires reset-password.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-identity-config/blob/74480722e1cc8405b5e9b65ac7d7086ab7f4056d/src/realm.json5\n\n[re-aaa-values] re-aaa-values\nCore uses identity-config0.32, X509/OTP enabled, username/password enabled; X509_MFA false, inactivity flag unset, detailed-observability alertingdisabled. Insecure admin password generation disabled. Truststore includes UDS bundle and serviceaccount CA separately from configimage truststore.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/keycloak/chart/values.yaml\n\n[mpn-identity-values] mpn-identity-values\nCore1.14 chart default fields: realmInitEnv.SSO_SESSION_MAX_PER_USER=\"0\"; ACCOUNT_INACTIVITY_DAYS unset; terms enabled unset; detailedObservability.alerts.enabled=false; realmAuthFlows username/password/X509/OTPtrue, X509MFAfalse. Gallatin owns these settings on MPN, independent of DU managedIL5/IL6 clusters.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/keycloak/chart/values.yaml\n\n[mpn-identity-override] mpn-identity-override\nCore value sourcePath .keycloak.keycloak maps to chart root; bundle override path is packages[core].overrides.keycloak.keycloak.values[].path (e.g.realmInitEnv), not Horizonpackageapplication values.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/keycloak/common/zarf.yaml",
          "finding_details": "Recommendation: Needs N/A justification. Delivered Horizon delegates all human identities to shared UDS and defines no temporary-user creation/type or72-hour temporary-account lifecycle. Configure expiry at the shared identity provider where applicable. Record that temporary accounts are prohibited/unused in the assessed realm; if they are permitted, the UDS operator must configure their expiration/removal.\n\nNext action: Record the temporary-account applicability policy; configure72-hour removal only if those accounts are allowed."
        },
        {
