          "comments": "Assessment recommendation: Needs N/A justification\nEvidence state: source-inferred\nAssessed release: 2026.45.4-uds.1\nHorizon commit: b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c\n\nJustification: At the assessed AAA provider boundary, default UDSrealm manages local users and the deliveredprofile selects no externalLDAP/directory authorization source. The official check applies only when AAA authorizations depend on externaldirectory services. Record that specific condition, and reassess any broker/federateddirectory override; ordinary OIDC delegation from Horizon does not prove an upstream temporary-directory authorization exists.\n\nComponents: UDS Core 1.14 shared Keycloak realm and Horizon OIDC clients; no bundled application Keycloak\n\nOwner: Gallatin SRE (self-managed UDS Core on MPN)\n\nNext action: Record assessed AAA boundary and whether an external authorization directory is configured; if yes attach72-hour temporary-authorization removal evidence.\n\nEvidence:\n[re-aaa-release] re-aaa-release\nSuccessful UDS publication artifact horizon-release-2026.45.4-uds.1 platform-contract.json selects identity.mode=uds, issuer https://sso.uds.dev/realms/uds, Core1.14.0; build-info.json enumerates12 deliveredimages and no bundled Keycloak.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon-uds-bundle/actions/runs/42114745685\n\n[re-aaa-realm] re-aaa-realm\nRealm has failureFactor3, permanentLockout true, maxTemporaryLockouts0; password length15,upper/lower/digit,special2,history5 and expiry60days; jsonlog listener emits user/admin events. Browser has password and X509 alternative authentication; X509MFA defaultdisabled. Account-inactivity workflow optionaldisabled; no minimum-age/difference/blacklist policy selected. Recovery flow requires reset-password.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-identity-config/blob/74480722e1cc8405b5e9b65ac7d7086ab7f4056d/src/realm.json5\n\n[re-aaa-values] re-aaa-values\nCore uses identity-config0.32, X509/OTP enabled, username/password enabled; X509_MFA false, inactivity flag unset, detailed-observability alertingdisabled. Insecure admin password generation disabled. Truststore includes UDS bundle and serviceaccount CA separately from configimage truststore.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/keycloak/chart/values.yaml\n\n[mpn-identity-values] mpn-identity-values\nCore1.14 chart default fields: realmInitEnv.SSO_SESSION_MAX_PER_USER=\"0\"; ACCOUNT_INACTIVITY_DAYS unset; terms enabled unset; detailedObservability.alerts.enabled=false; realmAuthFlows username/password/X509/OTPtrue, X509MFAfalse. Gallatin owns these settings on MPN, independent of DU managedIL5/IL6 clusters.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/keycloak/chart/values.yaml\n\n[mpn-identity-override] mpn-identity-override\nCore value sourcePath .keycloak.keycloak maps to chart root; bundle override path is packages[core].overrides.keycloak.keycloak.values[].path (e.g.realmInitEnv), not Horizonpackageapplication values.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/keycloak/common/zarf.yaml",
          "finding_details": "Recommendation: Needs N/A justification. At the assessed AAA provider boundary, default UDSrealm manages local users and the deliveredprofile selects no externalLDAP/directory authorization source. The official check applies only when AAA authorizations depend on externaldirectory services. Record that specific condition, and reassess any broker/federateddirectory override; ordinary OIDC delegation from Horizon does not prove an upstream temporary-directory authorization exists.\n\nNext action: Record assessed AAA boundary and whether an external authorization directory is configured; if yes attach72-hour temporary-authorization removal evidence."
        },
        {
          "group_id_src": "V-204639",
          "group_tree": [
            {
              "id": "V-204639",
              "title": "SRG-APP-000025",
              "description": "<GroupDescription></GroupDescription>"
            }
          ],
          "group_id": "V-204639",
          "severity": "medium",
          "group_title": "SRG-APP-000025",
          "rule_id_src": "SV-204639r960774_rule",
          "rule_id": "SV-204639r960774",
          "rule_version": "SRG-APP-000025-AAA-000080",
          "rule_title": "AAA Services must be configured to automatically disable accounts after a 35-day period of account inactivity.",
          "fix_text": "Configure AAA Services to automatically disable accounts after a 35-day period of account inactivity.",
          "weight": "10.0",
          "check_content": "If AAA Services rely on directory services for user account management, this is not applicable and the connected directory services must perform this function. \n\nVerify AAA Services are configured to automatically disable accounts after a 35-day period of account inactivity.\n\nIf the AAA Services configuration does not automatically disable accounts after a 35-day period of account inactivity, this is a finding.",
          "check_content_ref": {
            "href": "AAA_Services_SRG.xml",
            "name": "M"
          },
          "classification": "Unclassified",
          "discussion": "Attackers that are able to exploit an inactive account can potentially obtain and maintain undetected access to an application. Owners of inactive accounts will not notice if unauthorized access to their user account has been obtained. Applications need to track periods of user inactivity and disable accounts after 35 days of inactivity. Such a process greatly reduces the risk that accounts will be hijacked, leading to a data compromise. \n\nThis policy does not apply to either emergency accounts or an infrequently used account (e.g., account of last resort). Infrequently used accounts are local logon administrator accounts used by system administrators when network or normal logon/access is not available. Emergency accounts are administrator accounts created in response to crisis situations.",
          "false_positives": "",
          "false_negatives": "",
          "documentable": "false",
          "security_override_guidance": "",
          "potential_impacts": "",
          "third_party_tools": "",
          "ia_controls": "",
          "responsibility": "",
          "mitigations": "",
          "mitigation_control": "",
          "legacy_ids": [
            "SV-95537",
            "V-80827"
          ],
          "ccis": [
            "CCI-000017"
          ],
          "reference_identifier": "2896",
          "uuid": "077fd654-3232-538f-bf09-0cb0e0aeed49",
          "stig_uuid": "48d52574-4cd5-5714-881e-63304d1f3ea9",
          "status": "open",
          "overrides": {},
          "comments": "Assessment recommendation: Needs work\nEvidence state: source-inferred\nAssessed release: 2026.45.4-uds.1\nHorizon commit: b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c\n\nJustification: Delivered path is sharedUDS, not bundledHorizon. Core supplies a disable-inactive-users workflow with35-day default, but workflow enabled flag is false unless ACCOUNT_INACTIVITY_DAYS is selected. No releaseprofile sets that platform override. This is a small UDS identity configuration/inheritance item, not a new application lifecycle service. Inactivity implementation already exists in Core and is Gallatin-operated; the source-known disabled default needs Gallatin configuration, not documentation from an external provider. Human review on 2026-11-10 confirmed Needs work under the instruction to apply the same 35-day inactivity decision to similar requirements. Share V-222411 configuration and verification work; confirm current configuration first and preserve only applicable authorized exceptions. The user-account workflow alone does not establish coverage for every group, role or device identifier in broader rules.\n\nComponents: UDS Core 1.14 shared Keycloak realm and Horizon OIDC clients; no bundled application Keycloak\n\nOwner: Gallatin SRE (self-managed UDS Core on MPN)\n\nNext action: Verify current identity/directory inactivity controls and ownership, then configure the existing 35-day workflow for in-scope human accounts if not already enabled, coordinated with V-222411. Persist the Core override and update the existing realm through a controlled change where needed; verify effective disablement. Confirm permitted emergency/infrequently-used account exceptions against the exact rule and retain configuration and test evidence. Credit an existing compliant directory service only where supported by the rule and deployment evidence.\n\nEvidence:\n[re-aaa-release] re-aaa-release\nSuccessful UDS publication artifact horizon-release-2026.45.4-uds.1 platform-contract.json selects identity.mode=uds, issuer https://sso.uds.dev/realms/uds, Core1.14.0; build-info.json enumerates12 deliveredimages and no bundled Keycloak.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon-uds-bundle/actions/runs/42114745685\n\n[re-aaa-realm] re-aaa-realm\nRealm has failureFactor3, permanentLockout true, maxTemporaryLockouts0; password length15,upper/lower/digit,special2,history5 and expiry60days; jsonlog listener emits user/admin events. Browser has password and X509 alternative authentication; X509MFA defaultdisabled. Account-inactivity workflow optionaldisabled; no minimum-age/difference/blacklist policy selected. Recovery flow requires reset-password.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-identity-config/blob/74480722e1cc8405b5e9b65ac7d7086ab7f4056d/src/realm.json5\n\n[re-aaa-values] re-aaa-values\nCore uses identity-config0.32, X509/OTP enabled, username/password enabled; X509_MFA false, inactivity flag unset, detailed-observability alertingdisabled. Insecure admin password generation disabled. Truststore includes UDS bundle and serviceaccount CA separately from configimage truststore.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/keycloak/chart/values.yaml\n\n[mpn-identity-values] mpn-identity-values\nCore1.14 chart default fields: realmInitEnv.SSO_SESSION_MAX_PER_USER=\"0\"; ACCOUNT_INACTIVITY_DAYS unset; terms enabled unset; detailedObservability.alerts.enabled=false; realmAuthFlows username/password/X509/OTPtrue, X509MFAfalse. Gallatin owns these settings on MPN, independent of DU managedIL5/IL6 clusters.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/keycloak/chart/values.yaml\n\n[mpn-identity-override] mpn-identity-override\nCore value sourcePath .keycloak.keycloak maps to chart root; bundle override path is packages[core].overrides.keycloak.keycloak.values[].path (e.g.realmInitEnv), not Horizonpackageapplication values.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/keycloak/common/zarf.yaml\n\n[mpn-identity-inactivity] mpn-identity-inactivity\nSet realmInitEnv.ACCOUNT_INACTIVITY_DAYS=\"35\" before firstimport. Existingrealm: uds Workflows >disable-inactive-users enabled=true, disable-user stepafter35d; realm-admin excluded by shipped workflow. Source establishes exact operator action without asking DU to prove it.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/docs/how-to-guides/identity-and-authorization/configure-account-inactivity-disable.mdx\n\n[mpn-identity-init-only] mpn-identity-init-only\nrealmInitEnv and realmAuthFlows are initial realm import inputs. Existing realm is persisted in DB; redeploying Secret does not change it. Core documents equivalent Keycloak AdminConsole settings. Use controlled non-destructive AdminAPI/console update and persist the desired bundle override; do not advise tearing down production identity.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/docs/how-to-guides/identity-and-authorization/configure-keycloak-login-policies.mdx",
          "finding_details": "Delivered path is sharedUDS, not bundledHorizon. Core supplies a disable-inactive-users workflow with35-day default, but workflow enabled flag is false unless ACCOUNT_INACTIVITY_DAYS is selected. No releaseprofile sets that platform override. This is a small UDS identity configuration/inheritance item, not a new application lifecycle service. Inactivity implementation already exists in Core and is Gallatin-operated; the source-known disabled default needs Gallatin configuration, not documentation from an external provider. Human review on 2026-11-10 confirmed Needs work under the instruction to apply the same 35-day inactivity decision to similar requirements. Share V-222411 configuration and verification work; confirm current configuration first and preserve only applicable authorized exceptions. The user-account workflow alone does not establish coverage for every group, role or device identifier in broader rules.\n\nNext action: Verify current identity/directory inactivity controls and ownership, then configure the existing 35-day workflow for in-scope human accounts if not already enabled, coordinated with V-222411. Persist the Core override and update the existing realm through a controlled change where needed; verify effective disablement. Confirm permitted emergency/infrequently-used account exceptions against the exact rule and retain configuration and test evidence. Credit an existing compliant directory service only where supported by the rule and deployment evidence."
        },
        {
          "group_id_src": "V-204640",
          "group_tree": [
            {
              "id": "V-204640",
              "title": "SRG-APP-000026",
              "description": "<GroupDescription></GroupDescription>"
            }
          ],
          "group_id": "V-204640",
          "severity": "medium",
          "group_title": "SRG-APP-000026",
          "rule_id_src": "SV-204640r960777_rule",
          "rule_id": "SV-204640r960777",
          "rule_version": "SRG-APP-000026-AAA-000090",
          "rule_title": "AAA Services must be configured to automatically audit account creation.",
          "fix_text": "Configure AAA Services to automatically audit account creation.",
          "weight": "10.0",
          "check_content": "If AAA Services rely on directory services for user account management, this is not applicable and the connected directory services must perform this function. \n\nVerify AAA Services are configured to automatically audit account creation.\n\nIf AAA Services are not configured to automatically audit account creation, this is a finding.",
          "check_content_ref": {
            "href": "AAA_Services_SRG.xml",
            "name": "M"
          },
          "classification": "Unclassified",
          "discussion": "Once an attacker establishes access to a system, the attacker often attempts to create a persistent method of reestablishing access. One way to accomplish this is for the attacker to simply create a new account. Auditing of account creation is one method for mitigating this risk. A comprehensive account management process will ensure an audit trail documents the creation of user accounts and, as required, notifies administrators and/or managers. Such a process greatly reduces the risk that accounts will be surreptitiously created and provides logging that can be used for forensic purposes.",
          "false_positives": "",
          "false_negatives": "",
          "documentable": "false",
          "security_override_guidance": "",
          "potential_impacts": "",
          "third_party_tools": "",
          "ia_controls": "",
          "responsibility": "",
          "mitigations": "",
          "mitigation_control": "",
          "legacy_ids": [
            "SV-95539",
            "V-80829"
          ],
          "ccis": [
            "CCI-000018"
          ],
          "reference_identifier": "2896",
          "uuid": "1e39466d-23a5-5eef-b2c8-2b8f7a6bd5bf",
          "stig_uuid": "48d52574-4cd5-5714-881e-63304d1f3ea9",
          "status": "not_reviewed",
          "overrides": {},
          "comments": "Assessment recommendation: Likely covered\nEvidence state: source-inferred\nAssessed release: 2026.45.4-uds.1\nHorizon commit: b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c\n\nJustification: Actual shared UDS realm enables adminEventsEnabled/adminEventsDetailsEnabled plus jsonlog-event-listener. Account CREATE/UPDATE/DELETE operations, including enabled-state changes, therefore automatically emit admin audit records. These are shipped-provider functions rather than optional bundled forwarding. Required SA/ISSO notifications are a separate residual.\n\nComponents: UDS Core 1.14 shared Keycloak realm and Horizon OIDC clients; no bundled application Keycloak\n\nOwner: Gallatin SRE (self-managed UDS Core on MPN)\n\nNext action: Maintain the cited source/configuration mapping for the selected release and reassess any Gallatin deployment overrides that change this control.\n\nEvidence:\n[re-aaa-release] re-aaa-release\nSuccessful UDS publication artifact horizon-release-2026.45.4-uds.1 platform-contract.json selects identity.mode=uds, issuer https://sso.uds.dev/realms/uds, Core1.14.0; build-info.json enumerates12 deliveredimages and no bundled Keycloak.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon-uds-bundle/actions/runs/42114745685\n\n[re-aaa-realm] re-aaa-realm\nRealm has failureFactor3, permanentLockout true, maxTemporaryLockouts0; password length15,upper/lower/digit,special2,history5 and expiry60days; jsonlog listener emits user/admin events. Browser has password and X509 alternative authentication; X509MFA defaultdisabled. Account-inactivity workflow optionaldisabled; no minimum-age/difference/blacklist policy selected. Recovery flow requires reset-password.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-identity-config/blob/74480722e1cc8405b5e9b65ac7d7086ab7f4056d/src/realm.json5\n\n[re-aaa-json-events] re-aaa-json-events\nListener serializes user/admin identity events to stdout with actor/source/time/detail, suitable for UDS Vector collection; does not itself pushSA/ISSO notification messages.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-identity-config/blob/74480722e1cc8405b5e9b65ac7d7086ab7f4056d/src/plugin/src/main/java/com/defenseunicorns/uds/keycloak/plugin/eventListeners/JSONLogEventListenerProvider.java\n\n[mpn-identity-values] mpn-identity-values\nCore1.14 chart default fields: realmInitEnv.SSO_SESSION_MAX_PER_USER=\"0\"; ACCOUNT_INACTIVITY_DAYS unset; terms enabled unset; detailedObservability.alerts.enabled=false; realmAuthFlows username/password/X509/OTPtrue, X509MFAfalse. Gallatin owns these settings on MPN, independent of DU managedIL5/IL6 clusters.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/keycloak/chart/values.yaml\n\n[mpn-identity-override] mpn-identity-override\nCore value sourcePath .keycloak.keycloak maps to chart root; bundle override path is packages[core].overrides.keycloak.keycloak.values[].path (e.g.realmInitEnv), not Horizonpackageapplication values.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/keycloak/common/zarf.yaml",
          "finding_details": "Recommendation: Likely covered. Actual shared UDS realm enables adminEventsEnabled/adminEventsDetailsEnabled plus jsonlog-event-listener. Account CREATE/UPDATE/DELETE operations, including enabled-state changes, therefore automatically emit admin audit records. These are shipped-provider functions rather than optional bundled forwarding. Required SA/ISSO notifications are a separate residual.\n\nNext action: Maintain the cited source/configuration mapping for the selected release and reassess any Gallatin deployment overrides that change this control."
        },
