          "finding_details": "Shared UDS supplies CAC/PIV/X509 mechanisms. However default browser flow also allows username/password, the password branch requires OTP via chart-generated MFA_FLOW_ENABLED/OTP_FLOW_ENABLED=REQUIRED, while X509_MFA_ENABLED=false; no deliveredprofile requires smartcard authentication for the applicable privileged/nonprivileged paths. Required PIV/CAC enforcement remains a provider-policy choice, not missing application code. Core implements CAC/PIV/X509 and required OTP on password paths, but defaults still permit password alternatives. Gallatin owns the required-card flow policy.\n\nNext action: Gallatin configures the approved required-card authentication path in Core: X509_AUTH_ENABLED=true and, for a certificate-only policy, USERNAME_PASSWORD_AUTH_ENABLED=false and SOCIAL_AUTH_ENABLED=false; apply equivalent existing-realm flow changes through controlled AdminConsole/API. Preserve approved emergency access and distinguish privileged PIV-card eligibility from personal CAC. These are existing provider flows, not new Horizon authentication features."
