        {
          "group_id_src": "V-204663",
          "group_tree": [
            {
              "id": "V-204663",
              "title": "SRG-APP-000158",
              "description": "<GroupDescription></GroupDescription>"
            }
          ],
          "group_id": "V-204663",
          "severity": "medium",
          "group_title": "SRG-APP-000158",
          "rule_id_src": "SV-204663r960999_rule",
          "rule_id": "SV-204663r960999",
          "rule_version": "SRG-APP-000158-AAA-000420",
          "rule_title": "AAA Services used for 802.1x must be configured to uniquely identify network endpoints (supplicants) before the authenticator establishes any connection.",
          "fix_text": "Configure AAA Services for 802.1x identification and authentication to uniquely identify supplicants before the authenticator establishes any connection.",
          "weight": "10.0",
          "check_content": "If AAA Services are not used for 802.1x endpoint identification and authentication, this is not applicable.\n\nVerify AAA Services are configured to uniquely identify supplicants before the authenticator establishes any connection.\n\nIf AAA Services are not configured to uniquely identify supplicants before the authenticator establishes any connection, this is a finding.",
          "check_content_ref": {
            "href": "AAA_Services_SRG.xml",
            "name": "M"
          },
          "classification": "Unclassified",
          "discussion": "Without identifying devices, unidentified or unknown devices may be introduced, thereby facilitating malicious activity.\n\nFor distributed architectures (e.g., service-oriented architectures), the decisions regarding the validation of identification claims may be made by services separate from the services acting on those decisions. In such situations, it is necessary to provide the identification decisions (as opposed to the actual identifiers) to the services that need to act on those decisions.\n\nThis requirement applies to applications that connect either locally, remotely, or through a network to an endpoint device (including but not limited to workstations, printers, servers [outside a datacenter], VoIP phones, VTC CODECs). Gateways and SOA applications are examples of where this requirement would apply.",
          "false_positives": "",
          "false_negatives": "",
          "documentable": "false",
          "security_override_guidance": "",
          "potential_impacts": "",
          "third_party_tools": "",
          "ia_controls": "",
          "responsibility": "",
          "mitigations": "",
          "mitigation_control": "",
          "legacy_ids": [
            "SV-95607",
            "V-80897"
          ],
          "ccis": [
            "CCI-000778"
          ],
          "reference_identifier": "2896",
          "uuid": "7a44db39-15a0-5157-96ea-e70abefb8905",
          "stig_uuid": "48d52574-4cd5-5714-881e-63304d1f3ea9",
          "status": "not_reviewed",
          "overrides": {},
          "comments": "Assessment recommendation: Needs N/A justification\nEvidence state: source-inferred\nAssessed release: 2026.45.4-uds.1\nHorizon commit: b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c\n\nJustification: The assessed delivered AAA component is shared Keycloak OIDC web/CLI identity, not an 802.1x authenticator, RADIUS/TACACS+ device-login service or VLAN assignment service. These exact checks condition applicability on those network-access roles. Record that provider/component scope and assess actual network authenticators separately; do not build EAP or guest VLAN behavior into Keycloak.\n\nComponents: UDS Core 1.14 shared Keycloak realm and Horizon OIDC clients; no bundled application Keycloak\n\nOwner: Gallatin SRE (self-managed UDS Core on MPN)\n\nNext action: Record the network-AAA role exclusion in component applicability; reassess any separate 802.1x/device-management service.\n\nEvidence:\n[re-aaa-release] re-aaa-release\nSuccessful UDS publication artifact horizon-release-2026.45.4-uds.1 platform-contract.json selects identity.mode=uds, issuer https://sso.uds.dev/realms/uds, Core1.14.0; build-info.json enumerates12 deliveredimages and no bundled Keycloak.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon-uds-bundle/actions/runs/42114745685\n\n[re-aaa-realm] re-aaa-realm\nRealm has failureFactor3, permanentLockout true, maxTemporaryLockouts0; password length15,upper/lower/digit,special2,history5 and expiry60days; jsonlog listener emits user/admin events. Browser has password and X509 alternative authentication; X509MFA defaultdisabled. Account-inactivity workflow optionaldisabled; no minimum-age/difference/blacklist policy selected. Recovery flow requires reset-password.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-identity-config/blob/74480722e1cc8405b5e9b65ac7d7086ab7f4056d/src/realm.json5\n\n[re-aaa-sso-boundary] re-aaa-sso-boundary\nPlatformKeycloak admin/public ingress is separate, sanitized clientcertificate header forwarded from gateway; certificate access available but optional at default browser boundary.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/keycloak/chart/templates/uds-package.yaml\n\n[mpn-identity-values] mpn-identity-values\nCore1.14 chart default fields: realmInitEnv.SSO_SESSION_MAX_PER_USER=\"0\"; ACCOUNT_INACTIVITY_DAYS unset; terms enabled unset; detailedObservability.alerts.enabled=false; realmAuthFlows username/password/X509/OTPtrue, X509MFAfalse. Gallatin owns these settings on MPN, independent of DU managedIL5/IL6 clusters.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/keycloak/chart/values.yaml\n\n[mpn-identity-override] mpn-identity-override\nCore value sourcePath .keycloak.keycloak maps to chart root; bundle override path is packages[core].overrides.keycloak.keycloak.values[].path (e.g.realmInitEnv), not Horizonpackageapplication values.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/keycloak/common/zarf.yaml",
          "finding_details": "Recommendation: Needs N/A justification. The assessed delivered AAA component is shared Keycloak OIDC web/CLI identity, not an 802.1x authenticator, RADIUS/TACACS+ device-login service or VLAN assignment service. These exact checks condition applicability on those network-access roles. Record that provider/component scope and assess actual network authenticators separately; do not build EAP or guest VLAN behavior into Keycloak.\n\nNext action: Record the network-AAA role exclusion in component applicability; reassess any separate 802.1x/device-management service."
        },
        {
          "group_id_src": "V-204664",
          "group_tree": [
            {
              "id": "V-204664",
              "title": "SRG-APP-000164",
              "description": "<GroupDescription></GroupDescription>"
            }
          ],
          "group_id": "V-204664",
          "severity": "medium",
          "group_title": "SRG-APP-000164",
          "rule_id_src": "SV-204664r981554_rule",
          "rule_id": "SV-204664r981554",
          "rule_version": "SRG-APP-000164-AAA-000450",
          "rule_title": "AAA Services must be configured to enforce a minimum 15-character password length.",
          "fix_text": "Configure AAA Services to enforce a minimum 15-character password length. This includes randomly assigned passwords, shared secrets, and pre-shared keys.",
          "weight": "10.0",
          "check_content": "If AAA Services rely on directory services for user account management, this is not applicable and the connected directory services must perform this function.\n\nWhere passwords (to include randomly assigned passwords, shared secrets, and pre-shared keys) are used, verify AAA Services are configured to enforce a minimum 15-character password length. This requirement may be verified by demonstration or configuration review.\n\nIf AAA Services are not configured to enforce a minimum 15-character password length, this is a finding.",
          "check_content_ref": {
            "href": "AAA_Services_SRG.xml",
            "name": "M"
          },
          "classification": "Unclassified",
          "discussion": "Password complexity, or strength, is a measure of the effectiveness of a password in resisting attempts at guessing and brute-force attacks. Password length is one factor of several that helps to determine strength and how long it takes to crack a password. The shorter the password, the lower the number of possible combinations that need to be tested before the password is compromised. Use of more characters in a password helps to exponentially increase the time and/or resources required to compromise the password.",
          "false_positives": "",
          "false_negatives": "",
          "documentable": "false",
          "security_override_guidance": "",
          "potential_impacts": "",
          "third_party_tools": "",
          "ia_controls": "",
          "responsibility": "",
          "mitigations": "",
          "mitigation_control": "",
          "legacy_ids": [
            "SV-95613",
            "V-80903"
          ],
          "ccis": [
            "CCI-004066"
          ],
          "reference_identifier": "2896",
          "uuid": "f0810538-6fe5-5990-87f7-c2f4badc09fd",
          "stig_uuid": "48d52574-4cd5-5714-881e-63304d1f3ea9",
          "status": "not_reviewed",
          "overrides": {},
          "comments": "Assessment recommendation: Likely covered\nEvidence state: source-inferred\nAssessed release: 2026.45.4-uds.1\nHorizon commit: b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c\n\nJustification: Actual sharedUDS passwordPolicy sets length15; delivered Horizon delegates login to this provider. No duplicate minimum-length implementation is required in the API.\n\nComponents: UDS Core 1.14 shared Keycloak realm and Horizon OIDC clients; no bundled application Keycloak\n\nOwner: Gallatin SRE (self-managed UDS Core on MPN)\n\nNext action: Maintain the cited source/configuration mapping for the selected release and reassess any Gallatin deployment overrides that change this control.\n\nEvidence:\n[re-aaa-release] re-aaa-release\nSuccessful UDS publication artifact horizon-release-2026.45.4-uds.1 platform-contract.json selects identity.mode=uds, issuer https://sso.uds.dev/realms/uds, Core1.14.0; build-info.json enumerates12 deliveredimages and no bundled Keycloak.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon-uds-bundle/actions/runs/42114745685\n\n[re-aaa-realm] re-aaa-realm\nRealm has failureFactor3, permanentLockout true, maxTemporaryLockouts0; password length15,upper/lower/digit,special2,history5 and expiry60days; jsonlog listener emits user/admin events. Browser has password and X509 alternative authentication; X509MFA defaultdisabled. Account-inactivity workflow optionaldisabled; no minimum-age/difference/blacklist policy selected. Recovery flow requires reset-password.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-identity-config/blob/74480722e1cc8405b5e9b65ac7d7086ab7f4056d/src/realm.json5\n\n[mpn-identity-values] mpn-identity-values\nCore1.14 chart default fields: realmInitEnv.SSO_SESSION_MAX_PER_USER=\"0\"; ACCOUNT_INACTIVITY_DAYS unset; terms enabled unset; detailedObservability.alerts.enabled=false; realmAuthFlows username/password/X509/OTPtrue, X509MFAfalse. Gallatin owns these settings on MPN, independent of DU managedIL5/IL6 clusters.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/keycloak/chart/values.yaml\n\n[mpn-identity-override] mpn-identity-override\nCore value sourcePath .keycloak.keycloak maps to chart root; bundle override path is packages[core].overrides.keycloak.keycloak.values[].path (e.g.realmInitEnv), not Horizonpackageapplication values.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/keycloak/common/zarf.yaml",
          "finding_details": "Recommendation: Likely covered. Actual sharedUDS passwordPolicy sets length15; delivered Horizon delegates login to this provider. No duplicate minimum-length implementation is required in the API.\n\nNext action: Maintain the cited source/configuration mapping for the selected release and reassess any Gallatin deployment overrides that change this control."
        },
