          "group_id": "V-204678",
          "severity": "medium",
          "group_title": "SRG-APP-000177",
          "rule_id_src": "SV-204678r961044_rule",
          "rule_id": "SV-204678r961044",
          "rule_version": "SRG-APP-000177-AAA-000600",
          "rule_title": "AAA Services must be configured to map the authenticated identity to the user account for PKI-based authentication.",
          "fix_text": "Configure AAA Services to map the authenticated identity to the user account for PKI-based authentication.",
          "weight": "10.0",
          "check_content": "If AAA Services rely on directory services for user account management, this is not applicable and the connected directory services must perform this function.\n\nVerify AAA Services are configured to map the authenticated identity to the user account for PKI-based authentication.\n\nIf AAA Services are not configured to map the authenticated identity to the user account, this is a finding.",
          "check_content_ref": {
            "href": "AAA_Services_SRG.xml",
            "name": "M"
          },
          "classification": "Unclassified",
          "discussion": "Without mapping the certificate used to authenticate to the user account, the ability to determine the identity of the individual user or group will not be available for forensic analysis.",
          "false_positives": "",
          "false_negatives": "",
          "documentable": "false",
          "security_override_guidance": "",
          "potential_impacts": "",
          "third_party_tools": "",
          "ia_controls": "",
          "responsibility": "",
          "mitigations": "",
          "mitigation_control": "",
          "legacy_ids": [
            "SV-95641",
            "V-80931"
          ],
          "ccis": [
            "CCI-000187"
          ],
          "reference_identifier": "2896",
          "uuid": "76d2a52c-f20c-52d7-b8cd-b6ee9e75036a",
          "stig_uuid": "48d52574-4cd5-5714-881e-63304d1f3ea9",
          "status": "not_reviewed",
          "overrides": {},
          "comments": "Assessment recommendation: Likely covered\nEvidence state: source-inferred\nAssessed release: 2026.45.4-uds.1\nHorizon commit: b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c\n\nJustification: Actual sharedUDS dod-cac authenticator maps certificate SAN otherNameUPN to usercertificateIdentity using the CustomAttributeMapper, which establishes the certificate-to-individual account binding. API consumes the resulting signed subject identity.\n\nComponents: UDS Core 1.14 shared Keycloak realm and Horizon OIDC clients; no bundled application Keycloak\n\nOwner: Gallatin SRE (self-managed UDS Core on MPN)\n\nNext action: Maintain the cited source/configuration mapping for the selected release and reassess any Gallatin deployment overrides that change this control.\n\nEvidence:\n[re-aaa-release] re-aaa-release\nSuccessful UDS publication artifact horizon-release-2026.45.4-uds.1 platform-contract.json selects identity.mode=uds, issuer https://sso.uds.dev/realms/uds, Core1.14.0; build-info.json enumerates12 deliveredimages and no bundled Keycloak.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon-uds-bundle/actions/runs/42114745685\n\n[re-aaa-realm] re-aaa-realm\nRealm has failureFactor3, permanentLockout true, maxTemporaryLockouts0; password length15,upper/lower/digit,special2,history5 and expiry60days; jsonlog listener emits user/admin events. Browser has password and X509 alternative authentication; X509MFA defaultdisabled. Account-inactivity workflow optionaldisabled; no minimum-age/difference/blacklist policy selected. Recovery flow requires reset-password.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-identity-config/blob/74480722e1cc8405b5e9b65ac7d7086ab7f4056d/src/realm.json5\n\n[mpn-identity-values] mpn-identity-values\nCore1.14 chart default fields: realmInitEnv.SSO_SESSION_MAX_PER_USER=\"0\"; ACCOUNT_INACTIVITY_DAYS unset; terms enabled unset; detailedObservability.alerts.enabled=false; realmAuthFlows username/password/X509/OTPtrue, X509MFAfalse. Gallatin owns these settings on MPN, independent of DU managedIL5/IL6 clusters.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/keycloak/chart/values.yaml\n\n[mpn-identity-override] mpn-identity-override\nCore value sourcePath .keycloak.keycloak maps to chart root; bundle override path is packages[core].overrides.keycloak.keycloak.values[].path (e.g.realmInitEnv), not Horizonpackageapplication values.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/keycloak/common/zarf.yaml",
          "finding_details": "Recommendation: Likely covered. Actual sharedUDS dod-cac authenticator maps certificate SAN otherNameUPN to usercertificateIdentity using the CustomAttributeMapper, which establishes the certificate-to-individual account binding. API consumes the resulting signed subject identity.\n\nNext action: Maintain the cited source/configuration mapping for the selected release and reassess any Gallatin deployment overrides that change this control."
        },
        {
          "group_id_src": "V-204679",
          "group_tree": [
            {
              "id": "V-204679",
              "title": "SRG-APP-000231",
              "description": "<GroupDescription></GroupDescription>"
            }
          ],
          "group_id": "V-204679",
          "severity": "high",
          "group_title": "SRG-APP-000231",
          "rule_id_src": "SV-204679r961128_rule",
          "rule_id": "SV-204679r961128",
          "rule_version": "SRG-APP-000231-AAA-000610",
          "rule_title": "AAA Services must be configured to protect the confidentiality and integrity of all information at rest.",
          "fix_text": "Configure AAA Services to protect the confidentiality and integrity of all information at rest. AAA Services may leverage the capability of an operating system or require the use of a purpose-built module for this purpose. Potential locations include the local file system where configurations and events are stored or in a related database table.",
          "weight": "10.0",
          "check_content": "Verify AAA Services are configured to protect the confidentiality and integrity of all information at rest. AAA Services may leverage the capability of an operating system or purpose-built module for this purpose. Potential locations include the local file system where configurations and events are stored or in a related database table.\n\nIf AAA Services are not configured to protect the confidentiality and integrity of all information at rest, this is a finding.",
          "check_content_ref": {
            "href": "AAA_Services_SRG.xml",
            "name": "M"
          },
          "classification": "Unclassified",
          "discussion": "Information at rest refers to the state of information when it is located on a secondary storage device (e.g., disk drive and tape drive) within an organizational information system. Mobile devices, laptops, desktops, and storage devices can be either lost or stolen, and the contents of their data storage (e.g., hard drives and non-volatile memory) can be read, copied, or altered. Applications and application users generate information throughout the course of their application use.\n\nThis requirement addresses protection of user-generated data, as well as, operating system-specific configuration data. Organizations may choose to employ different mechanisms to achieve confidentiality and integrity protections, as appropriate, in accordance with the security category and/or classification of the information.",
          "false_positives": "",
          "false_negatives": "",
          "documentable": "false",
          "security_override_guidance": "",
          "potential_impacts": "",
          "third_party_tools": "",
          "ia_controls": "",
          "responsibility": "",
          "mitigations": "",
          "mitigation_control": "",
          "legacy_ids": [
            "SV-95643",
            "V-80933"
          ],
          "ccis": [
            "CCI-001199"
          ],
          "reference_identifier": "2896",
          "uuid": "e8581c2f-8c95-5955-b388-1ac3687fd4ad",
          "stig_uuid": "48d52574-4cd5-5714-881e-63304d1f3ea9",
          "status": "not_reviewed",
          "overrides": {},
          "comments": "Assessment recommendation: Likely covered\nEvidence state: source-inferred\nAssessed release: 2026.45.4-uds.1\nHorizon commit: b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c\n\nJustification: The official requirement explicitly permits OS or purpose-built protection instead of provider-local encryption. SharedUDS isolates identity service/admin interfaces, private key/config paths and database/storage access; MPN owns underlying OS/storage protection per scope. Recommend inherited platform/storage coverage with a named boundary, not adding duplicate Keycloak encryption. Actual storage/key policy belongs in the inheritance evidence packet and is not asserted as observed here.\n\nComponents: UDS Core 1.14 shared Keycloak realm and Horizon OIDC clients; no bundled application Keycloak\n\nOwner: Gallatin SRE (self-managed UDS Core on MPN)\n\nNext action: Attach the MPN/UDS identity database and node-storage confidentiality/integrity inheritance statement; record storage overrides.\n\nEvidence:\n[re-aaa-release] re-aaa-release\nSuccessful UDS publication artifact horizon-release-2026.45.4-uds.1 platform-contract.json selects identity.mode=uds, issuer https://sso.uds.dev/realms/uds, Core1.14.0; build-info.json enumerates12 deliveredimages and no bundled Keycloak.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon-uds-bundle/actions/runs/42114745685\n\n[re-aaa-security-isolation] re-aaa-security-isolation\nKeycloak runtime configured strictFIPS, dedicated serviceidentity and file/volume paths; sensitive data stored within protected service/persistent/externalDB boundary. OS/storage protection is inherited, not a requirement to add independent application encryption.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/keycloak/chart/templates/statefulset.yaml\n\n[re-aaa-values] re-aaa-values\nCore uses identity-config0.32, X509/OTP enabled, username/password enabled; X509_MFA false, inactivity flag unset, detailed-observability alertingdisabled. Insecure admin password generation disabled. Truststore includes UDS bundle and serviceaccount CA separately from configimage truststore.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/keycloak/chart/values.yaml\n\n[mpn-identity-values] mpn-identity-values\nCore1.14 chart default fields: realmInitEnv.SSO_SESSION_MAX_PER_USER=\"0\"; ACCOUNT_INACTIVITY_DAYS unset; terms enabled unset; detailedObservability.alerts.enabled=false; realmAuthFlows username/password/X509/OTPtrue, X509MFAfalse. Gallatin owns these settings on MPN, independent of DU managedIL5/IL6 clusters.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/keycloak/chart/values.yaml\n\n[mpn-identity-override] mpn-identity-override\nCore value sourcePath .keycloak.keycloak maps to chart root; bundle override path is packages[core].overrides.keycloak.keycloak.values[].path (e.g.realmInitEnv), not Horizonpackageapplication values.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/keycloak/common/zarf.yaml",
          "finding_details": "Recommendation: Likely covered. The official requirement explicitly permits OS or purpose-built protection instead of provider-local encryption. SharedUDS isolates identity service/admin interfaces, private key/config paths and database/storage access; MPN owns underlying OS/storage protection per scope. Recommend inherited platform/storage coverage with a named boundary, not adding duplicate Keycloak encryption. Actual storage/key policy belongs in the inheritance evidence packet and is not asserted as observed here.\n\nNext action: Attach the MPN/UDS identity database and node-storage confidentiality/integrity inheritance statement; record storage overrides."
        },
        {
          "group_id_src": "V-204680",
          "group_tree": [
            {
              "id": "V-204680",
              "title": "SRG-APP-000234",
              "description": "<GroupDescription></GroupDescription>"
            }
          ],
          "group_id": "V-204680",
          "severity": "medium",
          "group_title": "SRG-APP-000234",
          "rule_id_src": "SV-204680r971528_rule",
          "rule_id": "SV-204680r971528",
          "rule_version": "SRG-APP-000234-AAA-000060",
          "rule_title": "AAA Services must be configured to prevent automatically removing emergency accounts.",
          "fix_text": "Configure AAA Services to not automatically remove emergency accounts. Emergency accounts must not have automatic termination set.",
          "weight": "10.0",
          "check_content": "If AAA Services rely on directory services for user account management, this is not applicable and the connected directory services must perform this function. \n\nVerify AAA Services are configured to not automatically remove emergency accounts. Emergency accounts must not have automatic termination set.\n\nIf AAA Services are configured to automatically remove emergency accounts, this is a finding.",
          "check_content_ref": {
            "href": "AAA_Services_SRG.xml",
            "name": "M"
          },
          "classification": "Unclassified",
          "discussion": "Emergency accounts are administrator accounts that are established in response to crisis situations where the need for rapid account activation is required. Therefore, emergency account activation may bypass normal account authorization processes. If these accounts are automatically disabled, system maintenance during emergencies may not be possible, thus adversely affecting system availability.\n\nEmergency accounts are different from infrequently used accounts (i.e., local logon accounts used by system administrators when network or normal logon/access is not available). Infrequently used accounts also remain available and are not subject to automatic termination dates. However, an emergency account is normally a different account that is created for use by vendors or system maintainers, that is removed once the crisis has passed. When AAA Services do not perform account management, the connected Active Directory must provide this setting",
          "false_positives": "",
          "false_negatives": "",
          "documentable": "false",
          "security_override_guidance": "",
          "potential_impacts": "",
          "third_party_tools": "",
          "ia_controls": "",
          "responsibility": "",
          "mitigations": "",
          "mitigation_control": "",
          "legacy_ids": [
            "SV-95533",
            "V-80823"
          ],
          "ccis": [
            "CCI-001682"
          ],
          "reference_identifier": "2896",
          "uuid": "1d85a705-0fb1-5062-938a-b616aab2862e",
          "stig_uuid": "48d52574-4cd5-5714-881e-63304d1f3ea9",
          "status": "not_reviewed",
          "overrides": {},
          "comments": "Assessment recommendation: Likely covered\nEvidence state: source-inferred\nAssessed release: 2026.45.4-uds.1\nHorizon commit: b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c\n\nJustification: Actual shared UDS realm has no automatic account-removal policy; its optional inactivity workflow is disabled by default and explicitly excludes realm-admin users if enabled. Thus source does not automatically terminate the emergency administrative path. Record designated emergency accounts and ensure any new expiry/offboarding policy preserves approved exceptions.\n\nComponents: UDS Core 1.14 shared Keycloak realm and Horizon OIDC clients; no bundled application Keycloak\n\nOwner: Gallatin SRE (self-managed UDS Core on MPN)\n\nNext action: Retain the designated emergency-account policy and exclusions alongside any activation of inactivity/expiry workflows.\n\nEvidence:\n[re-aaa-release] re-aaa-release\nSuccessful UDS publication artifact horizon-release-2026.45.4-uds.1 platform-contract.json selects identity.mode=uds, issuer https://sso.uds.dev/realms/uds, Core1.14.0; build-info.json enumerates12 deliveredimages and no bundled Keycloak.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon-uds-bundle/actions/runs/42114745685\n\n[re-aaa-realm] re-aaa-realm\nRealm has failureFactor3, permanentLockout true, maxTemporaryLockouts0; password length15,upper/lower/digit,special2,history5 and expiry60days; jsonlog listener emits user/admin events. Browser has password and X509 alternative authentication; X509MFA defaultdisabled. Account-inactivity workflow optionaldisabled; no minimum-age/difference/blacklist policy selected. Recovery flow requires reset-password.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-identity-config/blob/74480722e1cc8405b5e9b65ac7d7086ab7f4056d/src/realm.json5\n\n[re-aaa-values] re-aaa-values\nCore uses identity-config0.32, X509/OTP enabled, username/password enabled; X509_MFA false, inactivity flag unset, detailed-observability alertingdisabled. Insecure admin password generation disabled. Truststore includes UDS bundle and serviceaccount CA separately from configimage truststore.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/keycloak/chart/values.yaml\n\n[mpn-identity-values] mpn-identity-values\nCore1.14 chart default fields: realmInitEnv.SSO_SESSION_MAX_PER_USER=\"0\"; ACCOUNT_INACTIVITY_DAYS unset; terms enabled unset; detailedObservability.alerts.enabled=false; realmAuthFlows username/password/X509/OTPtrue, X509MFAfalse. Gallatin owns these settings on MPN, independent of DU managedIL5/IL6 clusters.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/keycloak/chart/values.yaml\n\n[mpn-identity-override] mpn-identity-override\nCore value sourcePath .keycloak.keycloak maps to chart root; bundle override path is packages[core].overrides.keycloak.keycloak.values[].path (e.g.realmInitEnv), not Horizonpackageapplication values.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/keycloak/common/zarf.yaml",
          "finding_details": "Recommendation: Likely covered. Actual shared UDS realm has no automatic account-removal policy; its optional inactivity workflow is disabled by default and explicitly excludes realm-admin users if enabled. Thus source does not automatically terminate the emergency administrative path. Record designated emergency accounts and ensure any new expiry/offboarding policy preserves approved exceptions.\n\nNext action: Retain the designated emergency-account policy and exclusions alongside any activation of inactivity/expiry workflows."
        },
        {
