          "overrides": {},
          "comments": "Assessment recommendation: Likely covered\nEvidence state: source-inferred\nAssessed release: 2026.45.4-uds.1\nHorizon commit: b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c\n\nJustification: Actual shared UDS realm has no automatic account-removal policy; its optional inactivity workflow is disabled by default and explicitly excludes realm-admin users if enabled. Thus source does not automatically terminate the emergency administrative path. Record designated emergency accounts and ensure any new expiry/offboarding policy preserves approved exceptions.\n\nComponents: UDS Core 1.14 shared Keycloak realm and Horizon OIDC clients; no bundled application Keycloak\n\nOwner: Gallatin SRE (self-managed UDS Core on MPN)\n\nNext action: Retain the designated emergency-account policy and exclusions alongside any activation of inactivity/expiry workflows.\n\nEvidence:\n[re-aaa-release] re-aaa-release\nSuccessful UDS publication artifact horizon-release-2026.45.4-uds.1 platform-contract.json selects identity.mode=uds, issuer https://sso.uds.dev/realms/uds, Core1.14.0; build-info.json enumerates12 deliveredimages and no bundled Keycloak.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon-uds-bundle/actions/runs/42114745685\n\n[re-aaa-realm] re-aaa-realm\nRealm has failureFactor3, permanentLockout true, maxTemporaryLockouts0; password length15,upper/lower/digit,special2,history5 and expiry60days; jsonlog listener emits user/admin events. Browser has password and X509 alternative authentication; X509MFA defaultdisabled. Account-inactivity workflow optionaldisabled; no minimum-age/difference/blacklist policy selected. Recovery flow requires reset-password.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-identity-config/blob/74480722e1cc8405b5e9b65ac7d7086ab7f4056d/src/realm.json5\n\n[re-aaa-values] re-aaa-values\nCore uses identity-config0.32, X509/OTP enabled, username/password enabled; X509_MFA false, inactivity flag unset, detailed-observability alertingdisabled. Insecure admin password generation disabled. Truststore includes UDS bundle and serviceaccount CA separately from configimage truststore.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/keycloak/chart/values.yaml\n\n[mpn-identity-values] mpn-identity-values\nCore1.14 chart default fields: realmInitEnv.SSO_SESSION_MAX_PER_USER=\"0\"; ACCOUNT_INACTIVITY_DAYS unset; terms enabled unset; detailedObservability.alerts.enabled=false; realmAuthFlows username/password/X509/OTPtrue, X509MFAfalse. Gallatin owns these settings on MPN, independent of DU managedIL5/IL6 clusters.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/keycloak/chart/values.yaml\n\n[mpn-identity-override] mpn-identity-override\nCore value sourcePath .keycloak.keycloak maps to chart root; bundle override path is packages[core].overrides.keycloak.keycloak.values[].path (e.g.realmInitEnv), not Horizonpackageapplication values.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/keycloak/common/zarf.yaml",
          "finding_details": "Recommendation: Likely covered. Actual shared UDS realm has no automatic account-removal policy; its optional inactivity workflow is disabled by default and explicitly excludes realm-admin users if enabled. Thus source does not automatically terminate the emergency administrative path. Record designated emergency accounts and ensure any new expiry/offboarding policy preserves approved exceptions.\n\nNext action: Retain the designated emergency-account policy and exclusions alongside any activation of inactivity/expiry workflows."
        },
        {
          "group_id_src": "V-204682",
          "group_tree": [
            {
              "id": "V-204682",
              "title": "SRG-APP-000291",
              "description": "<GroupDescription></GroupDescription>"
            }
          ],
          "group_id": "V-204682",
          "severity": "medium",
          "group_title": "SRG-APP-000291",
          "rule_id_src": "SV-204682r981574_rule",
          "rule_id": "SV-204682r981574",
          "rule_version": "SRG-APP-000291-AAA-000130",
          "rule_title": "AAA Services must be configured to notify the system administrators (SAs) and information system security officer (ISSO) when accounts are created.",
          "fix_text": "Configure AAA Services to notify the SAs and the ISSO when accounts are created.",
          "weight": "10.0",
          "check_content": "If AAA Services rely on directory services for user account management, this is not applicable and the connected directory services must perform this function. \n\nVerify AAA Services are configured to notify the SAs and ISSO when accounts are created.\n\nIf AAA Services are not configured to notify the SAs and ISSO when accounts are created, this is a finding.",
          "check_content_ref": {
            "href": "AAA_Services_SRG.xml",
            "name": "M"
          },
          "classification": "Unclassified",
          "discussion": "Once an attacker establishes access to an application, the attacker often attempts to create a persistent method of re-establishing access. One way to accomplish this is for the attacker to simply create a new account. Sending notification of account creation events to the system administrator and ISSO is one method for mitigating this risk. \n\nAAA Services may not have built-in capabilities to notify the administrators and ISSO and may require the use of third-party tools (e.g. SNMP, SIEM) to perform the notification.",
          "false_positives": "",
          "false_negatives": "",
          "documentable": "false",
          "security_override_guidance": "",
          "potential_impacts": "",
          "third_party_tools": "",
          "ia_controls": "",
          "responsibility": "",
          "mitigations": "",
          "mitigation_control": "",
          "legacy_ids": [
            "SV-95547",
            "V-80837"
          ],
          "ccis": [
            "CCI-000015"
          ],
          "reference_identifier": "2896",
          "uuid": "4cce8bc5-8988-5cd2-90fe-5d6c5adddce7",
          "stig_uuid": "48d52574-4cd5-5714-881e-63304d1f3ea9",
          "status": "open",
          "overrides": {},
          "comments": "Assessment recommendation: Needs work\nEvidence state: source-inferred\nAssessed release: 2026.45.4-uds.1\nHorizon commit: b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c\n\nJustification: Delivered UDS JSON listener already emits the relevant user/admin events to centralLoki, so no Horizon eventforwarder is required. The remaining gap is narrower: Core modification alert rules are optionaldisabled by default, with no profile establishing SA/ISSO delivery. An auditable event/searchable dashboard is not a configured account-event notification route. Gallatin operates UDS monitoring and can enable shipped rules/receivers directly; DU managedclusters are a different authorization boundary. Human review on 2026-11-10 confirmed Needs work under the instruction to apply this decision to SA/ISSO account-change notification requirements. Source logs and optional alert templates do not establish notifications to the required recipients.\n\nComponents: UDS Core 1.14 shared Keycloak realm and Horizon OIDC clients; no bundled application Keycloak\n\nOwner: Gallatin SRE (self-managed UDS Core on MPN)\n\nNext action: Enable centralized account-creation notifications for the assessed component and configure named SA and ISSO recipients. Confirm that alert rules cover the relevant identity event; add or adjust a rule where the existing templates do not. Create a test account and verify notification reaches both recipients. Retain routing configuration and delivery-test evidence.\n\nEvidence:\n[re-aaa-release] re-aaa-release\nSuccessful UDS publication artifact horizon-release-2026.45.4-uds.1 platform-contract.json selects identity.mode=uds, issuer https://sso.uds.dev/realms/uds, Core1.14.0; build-info.json enumerates12 deliveredimages and no bundled Keycloak.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon-uds-bundle/actions/runs/42114745685\n\n[re-aaa-json-events] re-aaa-json-events\nListener serializes user/admin identity events to stdout with actor/source/time/detail, suitable for UDS Vector collection; does not itself pushSA/ISSO notification messages.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-identity-config/blob/74480722e1cc8405b5e9b65ac7d7086ab7f4056d/src/plugin/src/main/java/com/defenseunicorns/uds/keycloak/plugin/eventListeners/JSONLogEventListenerProvider.java\n\n[re-aaa-alerts] re-aaa-alerts\nOptional PrometheusRules alert on realm/user/admin modifications only if detailedObservability.alerts.enabled; rule availability is not configured delivery toSA/ISSO.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/keycloak/chart/templates/keycloak-logging-alerting-rules.yaml\n\n[re-aaa-values] re-aaa-values\nCore uses identity-config0.32, X509/OTP enabled, username/password enabled; X509_MFA false, inactivity flag unset, detailed-observability alertingdisabled. Insecure admin password generation disabled. Truststore includes UDS bundle and serviceaccount CA separately from configimage truststore.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/keycloak/chart/values.yaml\n\n[mpn-identity-values] mpn-identity-values\nCore1.14 chart default fields: realmInitEnv.SSO_SESSION_MAX_PER_USER=\"0\"; ACCOUNT_INACTIVITY_DAYS unset; terms enabled unset; detailedObservability.alerts.enabled=false; realmAuthFlows username/password/X509/OTPtrue, X509MFAfalse. Gallatin owns these settings on MPN, independent of DU managedIL5/IL6 clusters.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/keycloak/chart/values.yaml\n\n[mpn-identity-override] mpn-identity-override\nCore value sourcePath .keycloak.keycloak maps to chart root; bundle override path is packages[core].overrides.keycloak.keycloak.values[].path (e.g.realmInitEnv), not Horizonpackageapplication values.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/keycloak/common/zarf.yaml\n\n[mpn-identity-alerts] mpn-identity-alerts\nSet detailedObservability.alerts.enabled=true to create alreadyshipped Keycloak realm/user/admin modificationPrometheusRules. Logging/dashboards alreadyenabled. This is GallatinCoreconfiguration, not DU featuredevelopment.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/docs/how-to-guides/identity-and-authorization/configure-keycloak-notifications-and-alerts.mdx\n\n[mpn-identity-routes] mpn-identity-routes\nRoute via kube-prometheus-stack chart alertmanager.config.receivers/route, secretbacked notification credentials and uds-prometheus-config.additionalNetworkAllow matching endpoint. Gallatin must select actualSA/ISSO recipients; defaults cannot invent them.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/docs/how-to-guides/monitoring-and-observability/route-alerts-to-notification-channels.mdx\n\n[mpn-core-known-identity-settings] mpn-core-known-identity-settings\nKnown Core settings: realmInitEnv.TERMS_AND_CONDITIONS_ENABLED and themeCustomizations.termsAndConditions.text.inline/configmap; realmInitEnv.SSO_SESSION_MAX_PER_USER (default0 unlimited); realmInitEnv.X509_CRL_CHECKING_ENABLED/RELATIVE_PATH/ABORT_IF_NON_UPDATED; detailedObservability.alerts.enabled(defaultfalse), logging.enabled/defaulttrue. These are Gallatin configuration choices.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/keycloak/chart/values.yaml\n\n[mpn-core-account-alerts] mpn-core-account-alerts\nCore account/admin modification PrometheusRules are gated only on detailedObservability.alerts.enabled. Gallatin can enable them and configure recipients in its own Alertmanager deployment; vendor-provided proof is unnecessary.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/keycloak/chart/templates/keycloak-logging-alerting-rules.yaml",
          "finding_details": "Delivered UDS JSON listener already emits the relevant user/admin events to centralLoki, so no Horizon eventforwarder is required. The remaining gap is narrower: Core modification alert rules are optionaldisabled by default, with no profile establishing SA/ISSO delivery. An auditable event/searchable dashboard is not a configured account-event notification route. Gallatin operates UDS monitoring and can enable shipped rules/receivers directly; DU managedclusters are a different authorization boundary. Human review on 2026-11-10 confirmed Needs work under the instruction to apply this decision to SA/ISSO account-change notification requirements. Source logs and optional alert templates do not establish notifications to the required recipients.\n\nNext action: Enable centralized account-creation notifications for the assessed component and configure named SA and ISSO recipients. Confirm that alert rules cover the relevant identity event; add or adjust a rule where the existing templates do not. Create a test account and verify notification reaches both recipients. Retain routing configuration and delivery-test evidence."
        },
