          "group_id_src": "V-263538",
          "group_tree": [
            {
              "id": "V-263538",
              "title": "SRG-APP-000875",
              "description": "<GroupDescription></GroupDescription>"
            }
          ],
          "group_id": "V-263538",
          "severity": "medium",
          "group_title": "SRG-APP-000875",
          "rule_id_src": "SV-263538r981625_rule",
          "rule_id": "SV-263538r981625",
          "rule_version": "SRG-APP-000875-AAA-000220",
          "rule_title": "For public key-based authentication, AAA Services must be configured to implement a local cache of revocation data to support path discovery and validation.",
          "fix_text": "Configure AAA Services to implement a local cache of revocation data to support path discovery and validation.",
          "weight": "10.0",
          "check_content": "Verify AAA Services is configured to implement a local cache of revocation data to support path discovery and validation.\n\nIf AAA Services is not configured to implement a local cache of revocation data to support path discovery and validation, this is a finding.",
          "check_content_ref": {
            "href": "AAA_Services_SRG.xml",
            "name": "M"
          },
          "classification": "Unclassified",
          "discussion": "Public key cryptography is a valid authentication mechanism for individuals, machines, and devices. For PKI solutions, status information for certification paths includes certificate revocation lists or certificate status protocol responses. For PIV cards, certificate validation involves the construction and verification of a certification path to the Common Policy Root trust anchor, which includes certificate policy processing. Implementing a local cache of revocation data to support path discovery and validation also supports system availability in situations where organizations are unable to access revocation information via the network.",
          "false_positives": "",
          "false_negatives": "",
          "documentable": "false",
          "security_override_guidance": "",
          "potential_impacts": "",
          "third_party_tools": "",
          "ia_controls": "",
          "responsibility": "",
          "mitigations": "",
          "mitigation_control": "",
          "legacy_ids": [],
          "ccis": [
            "CCI-004068"
          ],
          "reference_identifier": "2896",
          "uuid": "4b4cdf38-48b4-552c-8d4c-34cda91694ac",
          "stig_uuid": "48d52574-4cd5-5714-881e-63304d1f3ea9",
          "status": "open",
          "overrides": {},
          "comments": "Assessment recommendation: Needs work\nEvidence state: source-inferred\nAssessed release: 2026.45.4-uds.1\nHorizon commit: b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c\n\nJustification: Actual UDS supports an explicit CRL file/cache path, but x509-cert-auth.crl-checking-enabled defaultsfalse and CRLdistribution-point checkingfalse. OCSP defaults enabled/failclosed, satisfying online revocation but not this distinct local-cache requirement. Configure cache or document approved offline/revocation tailoring at IdP. The cache implementation and delivery recipe already exist in Core; the shipped checking flag is off and Gallatin owns mounting/enabling/refreshing it. Human review on 2026-11-10 authorized applying the earlier non-platform decision to matching counterparts. Keep Needs work and share V-222553 verification/remediation where it covers this component. Preserve the exact component scope and applicability rather than treating a shared control as automatic compliance.\n\nComponents: UDS Core 1.14 shared Keycloak realm and Horizon OIDC clients; no bundled application Keycloak\n\nOwner: Gallatin SRE (self-managed UDS Core on MPN)\n\nNext action: Share V-222553 local CRL configuration, refresh/freshness controls and disconnected-validation tests. First verify current PKI-authentication paths and existing cache coverage for this component. Enable/update the existing shared IdP mechanism only where missing and retain effective configuration and valid/revoked/stale-data test evidence. Apply exceptions only where this exact rule supports them; do not copy an ASD-only exception to every component.\n\nEvidence:\n[re-aaa-release] re-aaa-release\nSuccessful UDS publication artifact horizon-release-2026.45.4-uds.1 platform-contract.json selects identity.mode=uds, issuer https://sso.uds.dev/realms/uds, Core1.14.0; build-info.json enumerates12 deliveredimages and no bundled Keycloak.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon-uds-bundle/actions/runs/42114745685\n\n[re-aaa-realm] re-aaa-realm\nRealm has failureFactor3, permanentLockout true, maxTemporaryLockouts0; password length15,upper/lower/digit,special2,history5 and expiry60days; jsonlog listener emits user/admin events. Browser has password and X509 alternative authentication; X509MFA defaultdisabled. Account-inactivity workflow optionaldisabled; no minimum-age/difference/blacklist policy selected. Recovery flow requires reset-password.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-identity-config/blob/74480722e1cc8405b5e9b65ac7d7086ab7f4056d/src/realm.json5\n\n[re-aaa-values] re-aaa-values\nCore uses identity-config0.32, X509/OTP enabled, username/password enabled; X509_MFA false, inactivity flag unset, detailed-observability alertingdisabled. Insecure admin password generation disabled. Truststore includes UDS bundle and serviceaccount CA separately from configimage truststore.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/keycloak/chart/values.yaml\n\n[mpn-identity-values] mpn-identity-values\nCore1.14 chart default fields: realmInitEnv.SSO_SESSION_MAX_PER_USER=\"0\"; ACCOUNT_INACTIVITY_DAYS unset; terms enabled unset; detailedObservability.alerts.enabled=false; realmAuthFlows username/password/X509/OTPtrue, X509MFAfalse. Gallatin owns these settings on MPN, independent of DU managedIL5/IL6 clusters.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/keycloak/chart/values.yaml\n\n[mpn-identity-override] mpn-identity-override\nCore value sourcePath .keycloak.keycloak maps to chart root; bundle override path is packages[core].overrides.keycloak.keycloak.values[].path (e.g.realmInitEnv), not Horizonpackageapplication values.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/src/keycloak/common/zarf.yaml\n\n[mpn-identity-crl] mpn-identity-crl\nCore includes an OCI CRL-volume packaging script and override example: mount current CRLs, set X509_CRL_CHECKING_ENABLED true and filepaths. Strictfreshness requires X509_CRL_ABORT_IF_NON_UPDATED=true; default examplefalse permits expiredCRLs. ImageVolume needs Kubernetes feature support; no customKeycloakcode/image required.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/docs/how-to-guides/identity-and-authorization/configure-x509-crl-airgap.mdx\n\n[mpn-identity-crl-script] mpn-identity-crl-script\nGallatin can package approved CRLs with supplied script and deliver updated OCI dataimage beforeCoreidentity component; mountreadOnly via chart extraVolumes/extraVolumeMounts.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/scripts/keycloak-crl-airgap/create-keycloak-crl-oci-volume-package.sh\n\n[mpn-identity-init-only] mpn-identity-init-only\nrealmInitEnv and realmAuthFlows are initial realm import inputs. Existing realm is persisted in DB; redeploying Secret does not change it. Core documents equivalent Keycloak AdminConsole settings. Use controlled non-destructive AdminAPI/console update and persist the desired bundle override; do not advise tearing down production identity.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/docs/how-to-guides/identity-and-authorization/configure-keycloak-login-policies.mdx",
          "finding_details": "Actual UDS supports an explicit CRL file/cache path, but x509-cert-auth.crl-checking-enabled defaultsfalse and CRLdistribution-point checkingfalse. OCSP defaults enabled/failclosed, satisfying online revocation but not this distinct local-cache requirement. Configure cache or document approved offline/revocation tailoring at IdP. The cache implementation and delivery recipe already exist in Core; the shipped checking flag is off and Gallatin owns mounting/enabling/refreshing it. Human review on 2026-11-10 authorized applying the earlier non-platform decision to matching counterparts. Keep Needs work and share V-222553 verification/remediation where it covers this component. Preserve the exact component scope and applicability rather than treating a shared control as automatic compliance.\n\nNext action: Share V-222553 local CRL configuration, refresh/freshness controls and disconnected-validation tests. First verify current PKI-authentication paths and existing cache coverage for this component. Enable/update the existing shared IdP mechanism only where missing and retain effective configuration and valid/revoked/stale-data test evidence. Apply exceptions only where this exact rule supports them; do not copy an ASD-only exception to every component."
        },
